  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "In a Circular City, there are nnn houses, numbered from 1 to n and arranged in 1,2,...,n,1,2,...\nChef needs to deliver packages to mmm (m&lt;=n) houses.\n\nChef is initially at house 1. Chef decides an integer xxx and stops after every xxx houses. i.e- if n=7n=7n=7 and x=2x=2x=2. He will stop at 1,3,5,7,2,... He may deliver a package when he stops at a house. His work is done when all the packages are delivered.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of times Chef has to stop, if he can choose any xxx ?\n\n**Note**: Starting point (1) is also counted in number of stops\n\n###Input:\n\n\nFirst line will contain n,mn, mn,m, denoting number of houses and number of packages respectively.\nNext line contains mmm distinct space separated integers denoting the houses\n###Output:\nSingle line containing an integer denoting minimum number of stops.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n3≤n≤10003 \\leq n \\leq 10003≤n≤1000\n1≤m≤n1 \\leq m \\leq n1≤m≤n",
